\section{Further results}
\label{app:further}

\paragraph{A rule for $k^*$ from training data (post hoc).}
Post hoc, we asked whether $k^*$ can be read off the training side: the excess over the floor of the designed run set in cross-validation on the training organisations alone. On the held-out organisations it matches the measured $k^*$ at 7 of 8 margins and is within one grid step at all 8, on the strength split it is within two steps at all eight, and on the temporal split (13 models) it is 2--6 grid steps too large. The training and test sides of the first split share a population, so we treat this as supporting evidence only.

